From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: coop-fetch <coop-fetch@localhost>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 02:00:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Co-op boss shots wrap: a boss's shooter create requests to
 the module

One more wrapped game function in patch 0005's table
(nx2/coop_world_wraps.py WRAPS; its id in host/hos_coop_boss_shots.h), for
oot-remake-multiplayer's row 222 (docs/dungeons-boss.md "Shooter
requests"):
- 11: main+0x374d20, the shooter's create request (shooter, shootable name
  hash, how many). The attack sequences' start step
  ActionSeqProcShootableActorCreate (main+0x746b48), the AI node
  OneShotShooterRequestCreateShootableActors (main+0x293ff98) and the
  shooter itself (main+0x378754) call it; it prepares the bullet a ranged
  attack throws.
Only the game whose own AI entered the attack ran it, so another game's
copy of the boss played the move with no bullet, or another variation's.
The owner's game runs it and the module sends each request; the other
games' copies make the same requests through the same function, whose own
calls for that boss the module skips there (phase 0 answers 1). Any other
shooter's requests run untouched. Nothing else changes: the wrap machinery,
the checks (build id, first words) and the hello's bits are 0005's.
---
 host/hos_coop_boss_shots.h | 21 +++++++++++++++++++++
 nx2/coop_world_wraps.py    |  5 +++++
 2 files changed, 26 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 host/hos_coop_boss_shots.h

diff --git a/host/hos_coop_boss_shots.h b/host/hos_coop_boss_shots.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..0000000
--- /dev/null
+++ b/host/hos_coop_boss_shots.h
@@ -0,0 +1,21 @@
+/* SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later
+   A boss's shooter requests, on Hookshot (oot-remake-multiplayer, docs/dungeons-boss.md "Shooter requests").
+
+   One wrapped game function more in the one wrap table (patch 0005's nx2/coop_world_wraps.py WRAPS; the ids are in
+   the one wrap space of hos_coop_world.h). Patch 0044 adds its row and this file (Hookshot's host/hos_coop_boss_shots.h
+   is the same file). The module's hos_coop_wrap gets it; Hookshot announces it in HOS_COOP_WORLD_HELLO's bits. The row:
+     (11, 0x374d20, (0x72001c5f, 0x54000260, 0x34000241, 0xb9402c09)),  # tst w2, #0xff; b.eq; cbz w1; ldr w9, [x0, #0x2c]
+   Phase 0 may return 1 (skip); the module then sets x0 to 1, the function's answer for a shootable it found. Phase 1
+   has its answer in x0. Plain C. */
+#ifndef HOS_COOP_BOSS_SHOTS_H
+#define HOS_COOP_BOSS_SHOTS_H
+
+/* main+0x374d20, the shooter's create request: x0 the shooter (an actor's component, [[actor+0x270]+0x3d8]), w1 the
+   shootable's name hash, w2 how many (the low byte). It finds the shootable in the shooter's table (+0x20, 0x38-byte
+   entries, count at +0x2c) and raises its asked count (entry+0x34, up to entry+8); returns 1 when found, else 0. A
+   leaf with no frame. Its callers: the attack sequences' start step game__bsa__ActionSeqProcShootableActorCreate
+   (main+0x746b48), the AI node OneShotShooterRequestCreateShootableActors (main+0x293ff98) and the shooter itself
+   (main+0x378754). It prepares the bullet a ranged attack throws. */
+#define HOS_COOP_WRAP_SHOOTER_REQUEST 11u
+
+#endif
diff --git a/nx2/coop_world_wraps.py b/nx2/coop_world_wraps.py
index 0000000..0000000 100644
--- a/nx2/coop_world_wraps.py
+++ b/nx2/coop_world_wraps.py
@@ -63,6 +63,11 @@ WRAPS = (
     # HOS_COOP_WRAP_PANE_ALIAS (patch 0042): the set-text of each pane of a layout with a matching alias (x0 the
     # pane, x1 a reference {+0 the text, +8 its length}). For the play-test bridge only, reads only
     (27, 0x377a990, (0xd503237f, 0xa9bc7bfd, 0xf9000bf7, 0xa90257f6)),  # pacibsp; stp x29, x30; str x23; stp x22, x21
+    # HOS_COOP_WRAP_SHOOTER_REQUEST (patch 0044): the shooter's create request (x0 the shooter, w1 the shootable's
+    # name hash, w2 how many): it prepares the bullet a ranged attack throws. A leaf with no frame; returns 1 when
+    # the shootable was found. The owner's game sends its boss's requests; the others' copies make them through
+    # this same function and skip their own boss's (phase 0 answers 1; phase 1 has the function's answer)
+    (11, 0x374d20, (0x72001c5f, 0x54000260, 0x34000241, 0xb9402c09)),  # tst w2, #0xff; b.eq; cbz w1; ldr w9, [x0, #0x2c]
 )
 
 
